<item>
            <title>[LU-20646] localrecov should take effect when clients reconnect</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20646</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Since patch &#8220;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12722&quot; title=&quot;exclude local client mounted on MDS/OSS from recovery&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-12722&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12722&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; target: disable recovery for local clients&#8221; landed for 2.14, local clients are excluded by default from recovery (by not making them part of &lt;tt&gt;last_rcvd&lt;/tt&gt;), unless the &lt;tt&gt;localrecov&lt;/tt&gt; server mount option is specified. This avoid impacting or delaying recovery in case of crash of a Lustre server that was also running a Lustre client, because this client will never be able to reconnect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But it looks like there are circumstances under which local clients are not excluded from recovery. For instance, if the client is mounted on the server &lt;b&gt;before&lt;/b&gt; a Lustre target is re-located on this server, it appears the relocated target will still make the now local client be part of &lt;tt&gt;last_rcvd&lt;/tt&gt;, hence not excluding it from recovery.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
